      "description": "Satellite images I've loaded from Australian Bureau of Meteorology and put them together in the animation. \nI images from 31 Jan. to 6 Feb. 2011.\nThey are 2 hours interval, and the latest images - 4  hours.\nI thought,  YASI is a girl's name. But apparently it is a Fijian name for the tree - Sandalwood. \nYasi - Sandalwood tree\nIt makes sense actually, as the cyclone is originated in  west of Fiji , where the cloud mass was formed at the end of January.\n\nInteresting how everything comes to a tree :)",
